  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does National Aeronautics and Space Administration spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $13B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The agency issued 7,317 awards with an average award size of $1.8M. Obligations were down 17.9% year over year and fiscal totals by year were $15B in FY21, $15.2B in FY22, $16.1B in FY23, $15B in FY24, $15.8B in FY25, and $13B in FY26."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does National Aeronautics and Space Administration buy?",
      "a": "NASA buys research, manufacturing, engineering, construction, and support services. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) totaled $4.9B, Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing totaled $2.4B, and other top categories include Engineering Services at $727M, Industrial Building Construction at $538M, and Facilities Support Services at $479M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are National Aeronautics and Space Administration's largest contractors?",
